{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsxsEpnayT6k91AxcUk8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The CLI is rewritten on Effect 4.1.2 and `npx tsc --noEmit` passes. I ran it against a local test server for every case in the spec, and all of them behave as asked.\n\n- **Success:** `1 USD = 0.9214 EUR`, exit 0.\n- **Unknown quote currency:** `unknown currency: XYZ` on stderr, exit 1.\n- **Invalid body:** `invalid response` on stderr, exit 2. This covers non-JSON, missing `rates`, and non-numeric rates.\n- **Retries:** a 500 on every request makes 4 requests in total (1 + 3 retries), with about 350 ms of backoff. Two 503s followed by a 200 succeed. A 404 is not retried.\n- **Other failures:** network errors and a missing `RATES_URL` exit 3 with a clear message.\n\nChanges are in `src/main.ts`, `package.json` and `package-lock.json`, plus the new `ANSWER.md`. I did not commit.\n\nDecisions you may want to change:\n- **Retry predicate:** I did not use `HttpClient.retryTransient`. It also retries 429 and 408, and the spec asks for network errors and 5xx only. I used `Effect.retry` with the same exponential schedule and a narrower predicate.\n- **Missing arguments:** these print the usage line and exit 3, under the \"any other failure\" rule. A conventional CLI would use a different code.\n- **Body read failures:** a connection dropped mid-body counts as an invalid response (exit 2).\n\nOf the colleague's note, I applied the v4 names, the bundled `ai-docs` example, the no-`@effect/platform` rule and the ground rules. I did not use `NodeRuntime`, since that needs `@effect/platform-node`. `ANSWER.md` lists each point and whether it applied. I did not verify the note's \"stable on 2026-10-01\" date."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":226,"cache_read_input_tokens":60582,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_toke